Article 7 The State shall implement classified management of environmental protection for construction projects according to the degree of their environmental impact, in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) Where a construction project may cause a significant environmental impact, an environmental impact report shall be prepared to conduct a comprehensive and detailed assessment of the pollution and environmental impact generated by the construction project;
(2) Where a construction project may cause a minor environmental impact, an environmental impact statement shall be prepared to analyze or conduct a special assessment of the pollution and environmental impact generated by the construction project;
(3) Where a construction project has a very small environmental impact and does not require an environmental impact assessment, an environmental impact registration form shall be completed.
The classified management catalogue for environmental impact assessment of construction projects shall be formulated and published by the competent department of environmental protection under the State Council after organizing expert demonstrations and soliciting opinions from relevant departments, industry associations, enterprises and institutions, the public, and other parties.

Article 8 An environmental impact report for a construction project shall include the following:
(1) overview of the construction project;
(2) current status of the environment surrounding the construction project;
(3) analysis and prediction of the possible environmental impact of the construction project;
(4) environmental protection measures and their economic and technical feasibility;
(5) analysis of economic gains and losses from environmental impact;
(6) recommendations for environmental monitoring of the construction project;
(7) conclusion of the environmental impact assessment.
The content and format of the environmental impact statement and the environmental impact registration form for construction projects shall be prescribed by the competent department of environmental protection under the State Council.

Article 10 The competent department of environmental protection under the State Council shall be responsible for approving the environmental impact reports and environmental impact statements of the following construction projects:
(1) construction projects of a special nature such as nuclear facilities and top-secret projects;
(2) construction projects that span the administrative regions of provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(3) construction projects approved by the State Council or approved by relevant departments authorized by the State Council.
The authority for approving environmental impact reports and environmental impact statements of construction projects other than those specified in the preceding paragraph shall be prescribed by the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government.
Where a construction project causes an environmental impact across administrative regions, and the competent departments of environmental protection concerned have disputes over the conclusion of the environmental impact assessment, the environmental impact report or environmental impact statement shall be approved by the competent department of environmental protection at the next higher level common to them.

Article 11 Where a construction project falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of environmental protection shall make a decision to disapprove the environmental impact report or the environmental impact statement:
(1) The type, site selection, layout, scale, etc. of the construction project do not comply with the environmental protection laws, regulations, and relevant statutory plans;
(2) The environmental quality of the area where the project is located has not reached the national or local environmental quality standards, and the measures proposed to be taken by the construction project cannot meet the requirements for the management of regional environmental quality improvement objectives;
(3) The pollution prevention and control measures adopted by the construction project cannot ensure that pollutant discharges meet the national and local discharge standards, or necessary measures have not been taken to prevent and control ecological damage;
(4) For reconstruction, expansion, and technological transformation projects, effective prevention and control measures have not been proposed for the existing environmental pollution and ecological damage of the project;
(5) The basic data in the environmental impact report or environmental impact statement of the construction project are obviously untrue, the content has major defects or omissions, or the conclusions of the environmental impact assessment are unclear or unreasonable.

Article 21 A construction unit that commits any of the following acts shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the Environmental Impact Assessment Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Commencing construction without submitting the environmental impact report or the environmental impact statement form of a construction project for approval or re-examination according to law;
(2) Commencing construction without the approval or re-examination approval of the environmental impact report or the environmental impact statement form of a construction project;
(3) Failing to file the environmental impact registration form of a construction project according to law.
